# L §2.3 `field = FIELD ":" (... | ref | ...)`; L §3.1 `key K`: "a key of index K, or a thing of kind K (§5.7)", and a
# movement is a thing of its event kind (§5.7); L §5.14 RC-7: the leaving rule's own example `if w in lot_outs and
# k.batch == w.lot then 0 else 1`.  An observed row's attribute `lot: key lots_in` names the observed row that started
# the batch, `lot: kb[k04]`.  kop holds batches kb[k03] (90) and kb[k04] (60), both of 2023-09-12, so `k.batch.day`
# ties them; the transfer kb[k06] of 60 names kb[k04] and takes it whole, and rza keeps its batch (L §3.6 "an arrival
# from a batched place keeps each part's batch").  q1: kop keeps kb[k03]'s 90 and none of kb[k04]; rza holds kb[k04]'s
# 60 (figures carried through).  q2: the attribute prints as rows print, and its field reads the movement it names.
# (Was LOAD-UNIT "a value of the wrong type for kb[k06]": loader.convert_value took no ref for a key type; the
# migrator.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2024-06-30
  start 2023-01-01
  end 2024-12-31

source s "test"
kind funds: unit
kind lots_in: event certain
  leg units: funds
kind lot_transfers: event certain
  leg units: funds
  attr lot: key lots_in
kind lot_holdings: holdings
  batched
  step 1
  takes k for w order (if w in lot_transfers and k.batch == w.lot then 0 else 1), k.batch.day
place kop: lot_holdings glb lives 2023-01-01..
place rza: lot_holdings glb lives 2023-01-01..
place world: outside lives 2000-01-01..
input kb: observed

ask q1: bal(kop, 2024-03-31) of kb[k03], bal(kop, 2024-03-31) of kb[k04], bal(rza, 2024-03-31) of kb[k04]
ask q2: o.lot, o.lot.day for o in lot_transfers over 2024-02-12..2024-02-12

version cast
  cite s
  known 2023-01-01
  funds + [glb] lives 2018-01-01..

version stmt
  cite s
  governs 2023-01..2024-12
  known 2023-01-01
  covers kop, rza
  opening[kop] = 0 at 2023-01-01 start
  opening[rza] = 0 at 2023-01-01 start
  kb[k03] = (on: 2023-09-12, kind: lots_in, leg units from world to kop amount 90 glb) "l3"
  kb[k04] = (on: 2023-09-12, kind: lots_in, leg units from world to kop amount 60 glb) "l4"
  kb[k06] = (on: 2024-02-12, kind: lot_transfers, leg units from kop to rza amount 60 glb, lot: kb[k04]) "l6"
=== expect
q1: (90 glb, 0 glb, 60 glb)
...
q2 (o = kb[k06]): (kb[k04], 2023-09-12)
...
